  "description": "T21-1b: a counted-loop index product (`i * n + k`) whose operands the enclosing loops prove nonnegative is lowered as a plain i64 `mul` guarded by one unsigned compare per operand against 2^26 (exact: the product is then below 2^52), and the invalid case folds into the sign bit the bounds check already rejects (`or` with valid-1). No flag-carrying `mulo`/`bo` pair or xor poison select may appear in the kernel. T22's S5.1.2-correct loop-condition slow edge may convert an unproven parameter lane to double elsewhere in the function; it is not part of this index product. Scoped to the proven arm 2026-09-13: the guarded `while` now emits a generic sibling whose canonical sentinel-aware lowering legitimately keeps the poison select (D2.2.2, D8.3.1); the forbid pins the proven arm, which is the kernel this fixture is about. Tune30 T30-1 (2026-09-18): the dense guard now versions the whole loop once, and its fast copy runs with the matrix extent (`n * n <= len`, overflow-checked at entry) assumed, so the pinned index product is a plain `mul`/`add` feeding a direct scaled load -- no per-operand 2^26 compares at all; those remain only in the generic copy.",
